    "PREAMBLE": "Wpcrl/276/2021 on 12 November, 2024\nAuthor: Manoj Kumar Tiwari\nBench: Manoj Kumar Tiwari\n2024:Uhc:8395 Office Notes, reports, orders or proceedings Sl.\nDate or directions Court'S Or Judge'S Order\nS No. and Registrar's order with Signatures WPCRL No.276 of 2021 Hon'ble Manoj Kumar Tiwari, A.C.J.\nThere is no representation for the petitioners.\n",
    "facts": "2. Petitioners have sought quashing of F.I.R. No.0025 of 2021, registered against them for offence punishable under Section 420 I.P.C. in Police Station Mukhani, District Nainital.\nThey have also sought a direction to the Police Authorities not to arrest them, pursuant to the aforesaid F.I.R.\n3.\nLearned State Counsel submit that, upon investigation, charge sheet has been filed against the petitioners on 16.03.2021.\n",
    "ANALYSIS": "Mere filing of charge sheet will not render the writ petition infructuous.\nWhether the allegations are true or untrue, would have to be decided in the trial.\nWhile exercising power under Article 226 of the Constitution, this Court is not expected to embark upon an enquiry into, whether there is reliable evidence or not.\nIt is not a case where FIR does not, disclose any offence.\nNone of the parameters laid down by Hon'ble Supreme Court, for invoking power under Article 226 of the Constitution for quashing an FIR, are met in the present case.\n7. In such view of the matter, there is no scope for interference with the impugned FIR while exercising extraordinary power under Article 226 of the Constitution.\n",
    "decision": "8. Accordingly, the writ petition fails and is dismissed.\n"
